1. Obtener el Resource ID de la Function App
az functionapp show \
  --name <FUNCTION_APP> \
  --resource-group <RG> \
  --query id -o tsv


2. Listar las métricas disponibles para un tipo de recurso en el CLI:
RESOURCE_ID=$(az functionapp show \
  --name <FUNCTION_APP> \
  --resource-group <RG> \
  --query id -o tsv)

az monitor metrics list-definitions \
  --resource $RESOURCE_ID \
  --output table

3. Consultar MemoryWorkingSet
az monitor metrics list \
  --resource $RESOURCE_ID \
  --metric MemoryWorkingSet \
  --interval PT1H \
  --start-time 2026-03-20T00:00:00Z \
  --end-time 2026-06-18T00:00:00Z \
  --aggregation Average Maximum
```[1](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cli/azure/monitor/metrics?view=azure-cli-latest)[3](https://github.com/MicrosoftDocs/azure-monitor-docs/blob/main/articles/azure-monitor/platform/rest-api-walkthrough.md)

